#: ../../administration/roles/roles.rst:4
msgid "Roles"
msgstr "Roles"

#: ../../administration/roles/roles.rst:7
msgid "Overview"
msgstr "Descripción general"

#: ../../administration/roles/roles.rst:9
msgid ""
"Within |morpheus| is a wide array of role based access control "
"capabilities. These roles can be managed within the Admin > Roles section"
" of the |morpheus| UI as well as through the API or CLI. They are "
"designed to be robust enough to fit within a wide array of enterprise and"
" managed service provider scenarios so they can be a bit hard to grasp at"
" first, but should make sense once a few simple concepts are explained. "
"There are two types of roles within |morpheus| called Tenant and User "
"based roles. Both sets of roles allow restrictions to be imposed on a "
"user at the feature access level. Entire sections within the appliance UI"
" can be hidden based on the specified access levels for features within "
"|morpheus|. Features have different access scopes that can be selected "
"from and can range depending on the specific feature. The most common "
"scope set involves none, read, and full. Instance Type access is also "
"common among both role types which allow the administrator to restrict "
"which service catalog items they are allowed to provision within "
"|morpheus| ."
msgstr ""
"Dentro de |morpheus| es a wide array de rol basado acceso control "
"capabilities. Estos roles puede ser gestionado dentro de el Admin > Roles"
" sección de el |morpheus| UI así como a través de el API o CLI. Ellos son"
" designed a be robust enough a fit dentro de a wide array de enterprise y"
" gestionado service provider scenarios so ellos puede ser a bit hard a "
"grasp en first, pero debería make sense once a few simple concepts son "
"explained. There son two tipos de roles dentro de |morpheus| llamado "
"Inquilino y Usuario basado roles. Both sets de roles permitir "
"restrictions a be imposed en a usuario en el acceso a características "
"nivel. Completo sections dentro de el appliance UI puede ser hidden "
"basado en el specified acceso niveles para características dentro de "
"|morpheus|. Características tienen diferente acceso scopes ese puede ser "
"seleccionado desde y puede range dependiendo de el específico "
"característica. El la mayoría de common alcance establecido involves "
"none, read, y full. Tipo de Instancia acceso es también common among both"
" rol tipos que permitir el administrator a restringir que service catalog"
" items ellos son allowed a provision dentro de |morpheus| ."

#: ../../administration/roles/roles.rst:11
msgid ""
"There are several handy tricks for creating new roles within |morpheus| "
"and users can be assigned more than one role. When a user is assigned "
"more than one role, permissions are granted by the role with the highest "
"level of scope access. This allows roles to be built with small subsets "
"of features and combined to grant different individuals relevant "
"permission control. With resource permissions (that is, all types of "
"permissions other than Feature permissions), a default access can be "
"given as opposed to a specific (Full or None) permission for any "
"resource. A specific permission will always supersede a default "
"permission regardless of whether it's more permissive or more "
"restrictive. In other cases (default vs default OR specific vs specific) "
"the more permissive access will be given."
msgstr ""
"There son several handy tricks para creando nuevo roles dentro de "
"|morpheus| y usuarios puede ser asignado más than uno rol. Cuando a "
"usuario es asignado más than uno rol, permisos son granted por el rol con"
" el highest nivel de alcance acceso. Este permite roles a be built con "
"small subsets de características y combined a grant diferente individuals"
" relevant permiso control. Con recurso permisos (ese es, todos tipos de "
"permisos otro than Característica permisos), a predeterminado acceso "
"puede ser given as opposed a a específico (Full o None) permiso para "
"cualquier recurso. Un específico permiso va a always supersede a "
"predeterminado permiso independientemente de whether ello's más "
"permissive o más restrictive. En otro cases (predeterminado vs "
"predeterminado OR específico vs específico) el más permissive acceso será"
" given."

#: ../../administration/roles/roles.rst:13
msgid ""
"It's also important to note that built-in Roles, such as the System Admin"
" \"Superuser\" Role carry no special prominence. For resource "
"permissions, the System Admin user has defaults set to Full in each "
"section. Thus, pairing the System Admin Role with another Role that may "
"include specific line item permissions for various resource categories "
"may cause your System Admin users to take on a reduced permission set."
msgstr ""
"It's también important a tenga en cuenta que built-en Roles, como el "
"System Admin \"Superusuario\" Rol carry no special prominence. Para "
"recurso permisos, el System Admin usuario tiene defaults establecido a "
"Full en cada sección. Thus, pairing el System Admin Rol con another Rol "
"ese puede include específico line item permisos para various recurso "
"categories puede cause su System Admin usuarios a take en a reduced "
"permiso establecido."

